Z||000000||SloPonti||09-15-1999||10:49 PM||||i have a 84 fiero and i am rebuilding a 2.5 liter out of a 84 celebrity!  i am putting in a different cam and i was wondering about what pistons should i put in it so i thought that i should ask you guys who have rebuilt a 2.5L-also has anyone heard of a header for this motor and if so were can i find one!  what about roller rocker arms? thanks for the help!  any other suggestions that might help this rebuild go better would also help!!!<BR>thanks again<BR>Rob||||reg||6
Z||000001||theogre||09-15-1999||11:15 PM||||Hmmmm....  I'd put the roller cam/lifter set out of an 86+ or it's performer equivalent in it. The roller lifters reduce cam load much more than rockers of any kind can.<P>Stay with a stock type rocker if you are changing the cam. You can change rockers later easy enough. This way you know what the cam is doing before you select rockers.<P>you need to keep the 2.5 close to stock compression. the block itself is not very strong. A slight over bore is ok, but odds are it will break if you go more than 20-30 thousandths over. This block it known well for rod punching. You want to make very sure that the crank and rods are in top condition. If there is any doubt at all replace the crank and/or the SET of rods.<P>Of course do as much porting/polishing as can be done. That alone will do as much or more than changing the cam and rockers.||||reg||2
Z||000002||88 Fiero||09-16-1999||10:23 AM||||Slo...there is a header available for the 2.5 Fiero at one time...Question is ...is it still in production...||||reg||1
